IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-67, TARGETED: the Tenants' Protection Law [Consolidated Version], 5732-1972. Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records four references of the Law (items I1 to I4) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: the individual to whom the Law applies, a tenant or a landlord. A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: a section as the instruments read give its status, a citation of sections, a citation of one subsection, and the questions asked of them. No reference is stated here; they are in tn67-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every citation is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument read.
-- Section numbers are written with Latin letters for the Hebrew ones the Law uses (52A is 52 alef); subsection letters are (a) alef, (b) bet, (c) gimel, (d) dalet, (e) he.
-- THE STATUS NAMES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's. A status is what the instruments READ give; the row says nothing about a section no instrument read touches except that no instrument read touches it.
-- NotChecked is a value, not an absence: it marks a section the citing words name and this row did not read (NOTES.md says which).

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A status in the current official text` IS ONE OF
    Present
    Repealed
    Deleted
    NotChecked

DECLARE `A subsection letter` IS ONE OF
    Alef
    Bet
    Gimel
    Dalet
    He

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page image`
    `official page image, with the consolidation agreeing (CONSOLIDATION-ONLY)`
    `official page image, with later instruments examined by name (see NOTES.md)`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`

DECLARE `A section` HAS
    `its number` IS A NUMBER
    `its added letter` IS A STRING
    `its status` IS A `A status in the current official text`
    `what the status rests on` IS A STRING
    `the printed date of the instrument that repealed it` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `A citation` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the sections the citing words name` IS A LIST OF `A section`
    `a later instrument read touches the citing words` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A range citation` HAS
    `the citation` IS A `A citation`
    `the range starts at` IS A NUMBER
    `the range ends at` IS A NUMBER
    `the numbers the range names` IS A LIST OF NUMBER

DECLARE `A subsection citation` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the section cited` IS A `A section`
    `the subsection letter cited` IS A `A subsection letter`
    `the subsections of that section as made` IS A LIST OF `A subsection letter`
    `the subsections of that section after the amending law` IS A LIST OF `A subsection letter`
    `a later instrument read touches the citing words` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `the instruments and pages read` IS A STRING

-- The questions. Each takes a value from tn67-cross-references.l4.

GIVEN s IS A `A section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section is in force` MEANS s's `its status` EQUALS Present

GIVEN s IS A `A section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section is repealed` MEANS s's `its status` EQUALS Repealed

GIVEN s IS A `A section`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the section was not checked or is in force` MEANS (s's `its status` EQUALS NotChecked) OR (s's `its status` EQUALS Present)

GIVEN s IS A `A section`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of the section` MEANS s's `its number`

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every section the citation names is in force` MEANS all `the section is in force` (c's `the sections the citing words name`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`every section the citation names that the row checked is in force` MEANS all `the section was not checked or is in force` (c's `the sections the citing words name`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some section the citation names is repealed` MEANS any `the section is repealed` (c's `the sections the citing words name`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the numbers the citation names` MEANS map `the number of the section` (c's `the sections the citing words name`)

GIVEN r IS A `A range citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no section the range names is repealed` MEANS NOT (`some section the citation names is repealed` (r's `the citation`))

GIVEN r IS A `A range citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the sections listed carry the numbers the range names` MEANS `the numbers the citation names` (r's `the citation`) EQUALS r's `the numbers the range names`

GIVEN c IS A `A subsection citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cited subsection is among those in force after the amending law` MEANS elem (c's `the subsection letter cited`) (c's `the subsections of that section after the amending law`)

GIVEN c IS A `A subsection citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cited subsection is among those of the section as made` MEANS elem (c's `the subsection letter cited`) (c's `the subsections of that section as made`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`

GIVEN r IS A `A range citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs of the range citation hold` MEANS `both limbs hold` (r's `the citation`)

GIVEN c IS A `A subsection citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs of the subsection citation hold` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`

-- The day a repeal took effect is not given by the pages this row reads (a printed date of an issue is not a day of effect), so the answer is NOTHING for every section.
GIVEN s IS A `A section`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the repeal of the section took effect` MEANS NOTHING
